hypothesis": "Lowering parameter_spread weight will reduce proxy-driven collapse (currently narrow stds ~0.003), increasing effective selection pressure toward performance and enabling exploration/exploitation that may find higher-performance designs.", "validation_plan_suggested_by_judge": "Run the next iteration and check for: (a) increased emphasis on higher-performance candidates (increase in mean or best performance vs current mean 0.0057 / best 0.0100), and (b) either increased diversity in parameter/performance space or clear upward trend in performance. Acceptance test will automatically compare post-change results to the current accepted state.", "self_reported_confidence_uncalibrated": 0.6, "target_assessment": null}, "notes": [], "judge_raw_output": "The analyzer shows the optimizer is being driven by the two proxy objectives (both weight=0.3) while true performance is near zero (mean 0.0057, best 0.01). Reducing proxy influence is the highest-leverage, low-risk change next. I will lower the weight of the parameter_spread proxy so selection is less dominated by that proxy and the optimizer can prioritize actual performance.\n\n<decision>\n{\n  \"failure_location\": \"objective\",\n  \"root_cause_hypothesis\": \"Optimization is being dominated by the two auxiliary proxy objectives (distance_from_center and parameter_spread at weight=0.3), causing premature convergence in proxy space and preventing meaningful selection on true performance (performance mean 0.0057, best 0.0100). I am moderately confident but unsure whether both proxies must be reduced immediately; changing one is a minimal, targeted step.\",\n  \"intervention_target\": \"objective\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Analyzer shows tight clustering on proxies (distance_from_center mean 0.3653 \u00b1 0.0037, parameter_spread mean 0.3643 \u00b1 0.0032) while performance remains extremely low (mean 0.0057, best 0.0100). Reducing parameter_spread weight from 0.3 to 0.05 should reduce its selection pressure and help the population redirect search toward improving the true performance objective without a larger invasive change.\",\n  \"proposed_change\": {\n    \"ops\": [\n      {\n        \"op\": \"set_weight\",\n        \"name\": \"parameter_spread\",\n        \"weight\": 0.05\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_benefit\": \"Lowering parameter_spread weight will reduce proxy-driven collapse (currently narrow stds ~0.003), increasing effective selection pressure toward performance and enabling exploration/exploitation that may find higher-performance designs.\",\n  \"validation_plan\": \"Run the next iteration and check for: (a) increased emphasis on higher-performance candidates (increase in mean or best performance vs current mean 0.0057 / best 0.0100), and (b) either increased diversity in parameter/performance space or clear upward trend in performance. Acceptance test will automatically compare post-change results to the current accepted state.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.6\n}\n</decision>", "change_id": "9ed52fd3621bd5eb", "candidate_state": {"version": 0, "planner_guidance": null, "objective_ops": [{"op": "set_weight", "name": "parameter_spread", "weight": 0.05}], "implementation_patches": {}, "workflow_params": {}}, "validation": {"seeds": [3000, 3001], "use_planner": false, "mode": "sequential", "max_stages": 3, "candidate_objectives": ["performance", "distance_from_center", "parameter_spread"], "baseline_objectives": ["performance", "distance_from_center", "parameter_spread"], "baseline": [0.009611342548472917, 0.009611342548472917], "candidate": [0.009611342548472917, 0.009611342548472917], "baseline_mean": 0.009611342548472917, "candidate_mean": 0.009611342548472917, "delta": 0.0, "min_improvement": 0.02, "candidate_constraint_violation": false, "details": {"baseline": [{"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 0.009611342548472917, "population_mean": 0.009611342548472917, "best": 0.009611342548472917, "n_invalid": 0}, {"split": "validation", "